cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis, its data or its analysis plan, please cite it as below."
title: "Who misses the TB nutrition payment, and where it matters most: a pre-registered State-level analysis of the Ni-kshay Poshan Yojana payment chain"
abstract: >-
  Code, extracted data, outputs and a pre-registered analysis plan for a State-level
  analysis of the payment chain of India's Ni-kshay Poshan Yojana, the monthly nutrition
  transfer to notified people with TB. For each State and UT it counts the people not paid
  at least once, shows whether they are lost before bank details or after, classes each
  unit's shortfall as account-led, payment-led or mixed, gives tiers rather than ranks
  (the unpaid count, and the count weighted by a relative need weight from NFHS-5 adult
  underweight), and reports an illustrative budget. It tests, as associations across
  units, whether coverage goes with the need weight, with the private-sector share of
  notifications, and with DS-TB treatment outcomes. It uses published, aggregate India TB
  Report tables (data years 2021, 2022 and 2023) and NFHS-5 fact sheets. Observational;
  no causal estimates.
